# 123corp-hr-leave-policy-reference

Authoritative 123 Corp leave policy constants and rules (vacation tiers, sick leave cap, bereavement, holidays, pay status requirements) a Jeffrey-agent must apply verbatim when answering employee questions.

## Conventions
- Pay cadence: biweekly (26 pay periods/year) — derived from accrual math.
- Vacation tiers (section 7.01): 0-1 yr = 40 hrs/yr (1.54 hrs/period); 2-4 yrs = 80 hrs/yr (3.08 hrs/period); 5-9 yrs = 120 hrs/yr (4.62 hrs/period); 10+ yrs = 160 hrs/yr (6.15 hrs/period).
- Vacation eligibility: earned from first full month; usable after 3 months of employment.
- Vacation accrual maximum: 2× annual earned amount; hours above max are lost.
- Minimum vacation use: 1 hour (non-exempt); 1 full day (exempt).
- Leave requests of 1 week or more must be submitted in writing 30 days in advance.
- Sick leave (section 7.02): accrues at 2 hrs/pay-period from date of hire; max 160 hours; may not be used before accrual or in lieu of vacation.
- Modified Duty assignments are capped at 3 months without review (section 7.02).
- Bereavement (section 7.03): up to 3 paid days for immediate family death; manager may authorize additional accrued sick or vacation leave.
- Leave Without Pay (section 7.04): requires manager approval; employee may be required to exhaust all paid leave first; unpaid absence >30 calendar days shifts anniversary date.
- Jury Duty (section 7.05): paid; employee must sign over jury/witness pay to 123 Corp (except travel reimbursement); must report to work during court breaks.
- Military Training Leave (section 7.06): up to 15 paid calendar days/year; beyond 15 days use comp time, then vacation, then unpaid leave.
- Paid holidays (section 7.07): New Year's Day (Jan 1), Memorial Day (last Monday in May), Independence Day (Jul 4), Labor Day (1st Monday after first Saturday in September), Veterans Day (if Nov 11 is a weekday), Thanksgiving (4th Thursday in November), Day After Thanksgiving, Christmas Eve (if Dec 24 is a weekday), Christmas Day (Dec 25).
- Holiday pay eligibility: employee must be on paid status the day before AND after the holiday.
- Non-exempt full-time employees who work a holiday receive 8 hrs holiday pay at regular rate PLUS 1.5× regular rate for all hours actually worked.
- Benefits (section 7.08): accrue normally on paid leave; suspended during unpaid leave.

## Assets
- 123corp-hr-policy-doc.md

